  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q005</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Which movement changes the beam angle while keeping the skin contact point approximately fixed?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Fanning (tilting) changes the beam angle from an approximately fixed skin contact point. Sliding moves the contact point to new anatomy, and deliberate overlapping slides also sample tissue. Good coverage combines overlapping translations with angular sweeps.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Sliding]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Compressing]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Rotating]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Fanning (tilting)]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q006</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A trainee is directly observed completing the right-lobe sweep in 20 seconds, storing only one image for the region. The most likely error is:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>An observed sweep that fast, covering that little ground, is far more likely to reflect sliding than fanning. A single stored frame does not itself prove incomplete coverage, but the observed speed and technique do.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Sliding when they should have been fanning]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Wrong preset]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Gain set too low]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Excessive compression]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q007</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Rotating the probe is the movement used to:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Rotation changes the scan plane - it is how you obtain the second orthogonal view of a lesion, and how you align the footprint within an intercostal space.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
